From: TwinQuill contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Fix TJS vector pop_back use with libc++

Kirikiroid2's custom vector wrapper previously returned the removed element,
but the current source resolves these calls to std::vector, whose pop_back()
returns void. Read the element first and then remove it.

Tested-by: tests/test_krkr_tjs2_source_admission.py focused git-apply unittest; forced Android CMake configure.

--- a/src/core/tjs2/tjsUtils.h
+++ b/src/core/tjs2/tjsUtils.h
@@ -485,5 +485,6 @@
 		_ensureCapacity();
-		int currentIndex = UnusedIndexStack.pop_back();
+		int currentIndex = UnusedIndexStack.back();
+		UnusedIndexStack.pop_back();
 		_tVectorList_Node &Node = PointerBuffPtr[currentIndex];
 		_tVectorList_Node &PrevNode = PointerBuffPtr[IteratorNode.prevIndex];
 		Node.Data = _Val;
@@ -515,5 +516,6 @@
 		_ensureCapacity();
-		int currentIndex = UnusedIndexStack.pop_back();
+		int currentIndex = UnusedIndexStack.back();
+		UnusedIndexStack.pop_back();
 		_tVectorList_Node &Node = PointerBuffPtr[currentIndex];
 		_tVectorList_Node &NextNode = PointerBuffPtr[IteratorNode.nextIndex];
 		Node.Data = _Val;
